IMPORT prelude

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 (Singapore) -- when I can be retired, and what my employer must offer me when I
-- reach my retirement age.
--
-- SEAT: the employee nearing, at or past retirement age.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 2(1) ("specified age"), s 2(2) (what counts as a dismissal), s 2(3) (attaining an age), s 4(1)
-- and s 7A(11) (the permitted ranges of the two prescribed ages), s 4(2)
-- (no dismissal on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age), s 6 (a lower contractual retirement
-- age is void), s 7(1), (2), (3) (eligibility for re-employment, the presumption of medical fitness, notice of an intention
-- not to re-employ), s 7A(1), (2), (6), (7), (9) (the duty to offer re-employment, working on past the specified age, the
-- length of a re-employment contract, retiring by choice), s 7B(1), (2) (what earlier service counts for), s 7C(1), (2)(a),
-- (b), (3), (4) (the employment assistance payment and taking up another employer's offer), s 11A (no contracting out).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/7/2022"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/RRA1993.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 38 of 2021, with effect from 1 July 2022.
--
-- THE ACT DOES NOT STATE THE AGES THEMSELVES. s 4(1) and s 7A(11) only fix the ranges (62 to 65; 67 to 70) within which
-- the Minister specifies the prescribed minimum retirement age and the prescribed re-employment age by Gazette
-- notification. No notification is deposited, so both ages are facts I state (they are on my employment record below),
-- and the worked cases use hypothetical values.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the officers (s 3); s 7A(3) (what the employer may do once I have worked on past the specified age) beyond
-- its effect noted at s 7A(2); s 7A(4), (5) (how the terms of a re-employment contract may vary); s 7A(10) (my notice of an
-- intention to retire); s 7B(3) (continuity); s 7C(2)(c), (5), (6), (7), (8) (the other employer's obligations in detail,
-- the amount of the payment, the consent form); the remedies and penalties (see rra-remedies.l4); exemptions, tripartite
-- guidelines and regulations (ss 11, 11B, 12) -- machinery.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the employee, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. It is not for public
-- use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 -- retirement and re-employment, from the employee's seat`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `The facts of my employment`

-- One case is one employment: me and the employer I work for under a contract of service (s 2(1): "any agreement,
-- whether in writing or oral, express or implied").
DECLARE `My employment` HAS
    -- s 2(3): I attain N years "on or after the Nth ... anniversary" of my birth, so this is my age in completed years.
    `my age`                                                                IS A NUMBER
    -- s 4(1): "the prescribed minimum retirement age" for my class of employees, set by Gazette notification (not
    -- deposited; I state it). The Act requires it to be 62 to 65.
    `my prescribed minimum retirement age`                                  IS A NUMBER
    -- s 2(1)(b) of "specified age": "the retirement age stipulated in the employee's contract of service", if any.
    `the retirement age stipulated in my contract`                          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    -- s 7A(11): "the prescribed re-employment age" for my class, set by Gazette notification (not deposited). 67 to 70.
    `my prescribed re-employment age`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `my year of birth`                                                      IS A NUMBER
    `my month of birth`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    -- s 7(1)(b)(i): the Act hands this judgment to the employer ("the employer assesses the employee as ...").
    `my employer assesses my work performance as at least satisfactory`     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(2): I am "presumed to be medically fit ... unless the employer ... proves, on a balance of probabilities"
    -- that I am not. So the fact is the employer's proof, not my fitness.
    `my employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that I am not medically fit` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7A(9), s 7C(3): "the employee's decision not to continue to be employed by that employer on or after the date
    -- the employee attains the specified age".
    `I have told my employer I will not continue working for it from my specified age` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7C(1): "unable to find a vacancy in E1's establishment that is suitable for the eligible employee, despite
    -- making reasonable attempts to do so in accordance with the tripartite guidelines". If I dispute it, the Minister
    -- decides (s 8B(6), (7)(b)); here it is the fact as it stands.
    `my employer cannot find me a suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7C(1)(b): "another employer (called in this section E2) offers to employ the eligible employee in lieu of E1;
    -- and ... the eligible employee accepts the offer", during my employment with E1.
    `I accepted another employer's offer to employ me in place of my employer` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `2(1) -- my specified age`

-- s 2(1): "specified age", in relation to an employee, means "the higher of" (a) "the employee's prescribed minimum
-- retirement age"; (b) "the retirement age stipulated in the employee's contract of service". Gloss: the age from which
-- my employer may retire me, provided it then offers re-employment. With no contractual age, it is the prescribed age.
GIVEN `my employment` IS A `My employment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my specified age` IS
    CONSIDER `my employment`'s `the retirement age stipulated in my contract`
    WHEN JUST `contract age` THEN `the higher of` (`my employment`'s `my prescribed minimum retirement age`) `contract age`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `my employment`'s `my prescribed minimum retirement age`

§§ `4(1), 7A(11) -- the ranges the Act allows for my two prescribed ages`

-- s 4(1): the prescribed minimum retirement age, "which must be at least 62 years but not more than 65 years".
-- s 7A(11): the prescribed re-employment age, "which must be at least 67 years but not more than 70 years".
-- The ages themselves are in Gazette notifications that are not deposited; this checks only that the ages I state for
-- myself are ones the Act could have set.
GIVEN `my employment` IS A `My employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the prescribed ages I have stated within the ranges the Act allows` IF
        `my employment`'s `my prescribed minimum retirement age` AT LEAST 62
    AND `my employment`'s `my prescribed minimum retirement age` AT MOST 65
    AND `my employment`'s `my prescribed re-employment age` AT LEAST 67
    AND `my employment`'s `my prescribed re-employment age` AT MOST 70

§§ `2(2) -- when I count as dismissed`

-- s 2(2): an employee "is treated as dismissed" if (a) the contract "is terminated by the employer, whether it is so
-- terminated by notice or without notice"; or (b) "the employer retires the employee, or requires or causes that
-- employee to retire or resign on the ground of age". Gloss: being retired, or pushed to resign because of age, is a
-- dismissal for this Act.
GIVEN `my employer ended my contract, with or without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my employer retired me, or required or caused me to retire or resign, on the ground of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as dismissed` IF
        `my employer ended my contract, with or without notice`
     OR `my employer retired me, or required or caused me to retire or resign, on the ground of age`

§§ `4(2), 6 -- no retirement before my prescribed minimum retirement age`

-- s 4(2): "Despite any other written law, contract of service or collective agreement, an employer must not dismiss an
-- employee on the ground of age before that employee attains the employee's prescribed minimum retirement age."
-- (The offence and its penalty, s 4(3), are in rra-remedies.l4.)
GIVEN `my employment` IS A `My employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer forbidden to dismiss me on the ground of age` IF
    `my employment`'s `my age` LESS THAN `my employment`'s `my prescribed minimum retirement age`

-- s 6: a term of a contract of service or collective agreement "which provides for a retirement age which is below the
-- employee's prescribed minimum retirement age is void to the extent that it is so less favourable". With no
-- contractual retirement age there is no term to strike down.
GIVEN `my employment` IS A `My employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the retirement age in my contract void` IF
    CONSIDER `my employment`'s `the retirement age stipulated in my contract`
    WHEN JUST `contract age` THEN `contract age` LESS THAN `my employment`'s `my prescribed minimum retirement age`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 11A: any term of a contract of service or collective agreement "is void insofar as it purports" (a) "to exclude or
-- limit the operation of any provision of this Act"; or (b) "to preclude any person from making a representation, a
-- claim or an application under this Act".
GIVEN `the term excludes or limits a provision of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term stops me making a representation, claim or application under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this term of my contract void for contracting out` IF
        `the term excludes or limits a provision of the Act`
     OR `the term stops me making a representation, claim or application under the Act`

§§ `7(1), 7(2) -- am I eligible for re-employment`

-- s 7(1): eligible if (a) "the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952"; and (b) "the employer assesses the employee as"
-- (i) "having at least satisfactory work performance"; and (ii) "being medically fit to continue working".
-- s 7(2): "presumed to be medically fit to continue working, unless the employer ... proves, on a balance of
-- probabilities, that the employee is not medically fit". Gloss: "eligible employee" (s 2(1)) is one who meets s 7(1).
GIVEN `my employment` IS A `My employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I born on or after 1 July 1952` IF
        `my employment`'s `my year of birth` GREATER THAN 1952
     OR (    `my employment`'s `my year of birth` EQUALS 1952
         AND `my employment`'s `my month of birth` AT LEAST 7)

GIVEN `my employment` IS A `My employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for re-employment` IF
        `Was I born on or after 1 July 1952` `my employment`
    AND `my employment`'s `my employer assesses my work performance as at least satisfactory`
    AND NOT `my employment`'s `my employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that I am not medically fit`

-- s 7(3): where the employer "does not intend to re-employ an employee because the employee does not meet the criteria
-- in subsection (1)(b), then as far as it is reasonably practicable, the employer must give the employee written notice
-- of that intention within a reasonable period before terminating the employee's employment". The Act sets no number
-- of days; "reasonable period" is left open, so this says only whether I must be given the notice.
GIVEN `my employer does not intend to re-employ me because of my performance or medical fitness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `giving me notice is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer give me written notice that it will not re-employ me` IF
        `my employer does not intend to re-employ me because of my performance or medical fitness`
    AND `giving me notice is reasonably practicable`

§§ `7A(1), 7A(9), 7C(1)-(3) -- what my employer must offer me`

-- s 7A(1): "Subject to section 7C, an employer must, before an employee ... (being an eligible employee) attains the
-- specified age, offer re-employment to that employee and the employer's obligation to re-employ that employee begins
-- from the time that employee attains the specified age, until that employee attains the employee's prescribed
-- re-employment age."
-- s 2(1) "re-employment obligations": "to re-employ an eligible employee in accordance with section 7A, failing which,
-- to offer the eligible employee employment assistance payment in accordance with section 7C(1)(a)".
-- s 7C(1): s 7A does not apply if the employer cannot find a suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts, and (a) it
-- offers an employment assistance payment, or (b) another employer offers to employ me in its place and I accept.
-- s 7C(2)(a), (b): then the first employer's obligations "are discharged immediately before the agreed date" and the
-- other employer stands in its place "from that agreed date".
-- s 7A(9): "an eligible employee may retire or be retired, if he or she does not wish to be employed by his or her
-- employer on or after the date the employee attains the specified age"; s 7C(3): no employment assistance payment need
-- be offered to an employee who has said so.
-- Gloss: "employment assistance payment" (s 2(1)) is the sum payable under s 7C(1) when no suitable job is found.
DECLARE `What I am owed` IS ONE OF
    `an offer of re-employment, made before I reach my specified age`
    `an employment assistance payment, in place of re-employment`
    `re-employment by the other employer, from the agreed date`
    `nothing, because I am not eligible for re-employment`
    `nothing, because I have said I will not continue`
    `nothing more, because I have reached my prescribed re-employment age`

-- Read with s 7C(1)(b): taking up another employer's offer displaces s 7A only where the first employer could not find
-- a suitable vacancy; s 7C(1) is written that way ("because E1 is unable to find a vacancy ... and ... (b)"). Where my
-- employer has a vacancy, it still owes me the offer.
GIVEN `my employment` IS A `My employment`
GIVETH A `What I am owed`
DECIDE `What must my employer offer me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Am I eligible for re-employment` `my employment`
            THEN `nothing, because I am not eligible for re-employment`
        IF `my employment`'s `my age` AT LEAST `my employment`'s `my prescribed re-employment age`
            THEN `nothing more, because I have reached my prescribed re-employment age`
        IF `my employment`'s `I have told my employer I will not continue working for it from my specified age`
            THEN `nothing, because I have said I will not continue`
        IF     `my employment`'s `my employer cannot find me a suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts`
           AND `my employment`'s `I accepted another employer's offer to employ me in place of my employer`
            THEN `re-employment by the other employer, from the agreed date`
        IF `my employment`'s `my employer cannot find me a suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts`
            THEN `an employment assistance payment, in place of re-employment`
        OTHERWISE `an offer of re-employment, made before I reach my specified age`

-- s 7A(1): the offer is due "before" I attain the specified age. Not eligible: no offer is due, so NOTHING.
GIVEN `my employment` IS A `My employment`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Before what age must my employer offer me re-employment` IS
    IF `Am I eligible for re-employment` `my employment`
    THEN JUST (`What is my specified age` `my employment`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 7A(1): the obligation runs "from the time that employee attains the specified age, until that employee attains the
-- employee's prescribed re-employment age".
GIVEN `my employment` IS A `My employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer's obligation to re-employ me running now` IF
        `Am I eligible for re-employment` `my employment`
    AND `my employment`'s `my age` AT LEAST `What is my specified age` `my employment`
    AND `my employment`'s `my age` LESS THAN `my employment`'s `my prescribed re-employment age`

§§ `7C(4) -- how the employment assistance payment is paid`

-- s 7C(4): the payment is "(a) a single lump sum payment paid by an employer by the last day of employment of the
-- eligible employee; or (b) other mutually agreed arrangements". Its amount follows the tripartite guidelines (s 7C(5)),
-- which are not deposited and not encoded.
GIVEN `my employer and I agreed another arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was paid as a single lump sum by my last day of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my employment assistance payment paid as the Act requires` IF
        `my employer and I agreed another arrangement`
     OR `it was paid as a single lump sum by my last day of employment`

§§ `7A(6), 7A(7) -- how long my re-employment contract must be`

-- s 7A(6): "Unless otherwise agreed by the parties to a re-employment contract, the period of employment stipulated in
-- the contract must not be less than one year at any one time."
-- s 7A(7): where the period from the start of re-employment to the date I attain my prescribed re-employment age "is less
-- than one year, the period of employment under the re-employment contract may be for that shorter period".
-- Months are the unit here; the Act speaks of "one year".
GIVEN `months from the start of my re-employment to my prescribed re-employment age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the shortest re-employment term I can be offered, in months` IS
    `the lower of` 12 `months from the start of my re-employment to my prescribed re-employment age`

GIVEN `the term offered, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `months from the start of my re-employment to my prescribed re-employment age` IS A NUMBER
      `I agreed to a shorter term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the re-employment term I was offered long enough` IF
        `I agreed to a shorter term`
     OR `the term offered, in months` AT LEAST
            `What is the shortest re-employment term I can be offered, in months`
                `months from the start of my re-employment to my prescribed re-employment age`

§§ `7A(2) -- if I simply keep working past my specified age`

-- s 7A(2): where "an employee mentioned in section 7(1)(a)" (born on or after 1 July 1952) "continues, after attaining
-- the specified age, to work for his or her employer" and the employer neither re-employs nor terminates the
-- employment, then any right, privilege, obligation or liability under the old contract acquired, accrued or incurred
-- before the specified age "is not affected". (s 7A(3) lets the employer then re-employ me, or terminate me if I fail
-- the s 7(1)(b) criteria; not encoded beyond this.)
GIVEN `my employment` IS A `My employment`
      `I am still working for my employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my employer has re-employed me or ended my employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my rights under my old contract unaffected` IF
        `Was I born on or after 1 July 1952` `my employment`
    AND `my employment`'s `my age` AT LEAST `What is my specified age` `my employment`
    AND `I am still working for my employer`
    AND NOT `my employer has re-employed me or ended my employment`

§§ `7B(1), 7B(2) -- what my service before re-employment counts for`

-- s 7B(1): "Unless otherwise agreed", for rights under the re-employment contract, service under the previous contract
-- "is disregarded". s 7B(2): it "is to be reckoned" for (a) the minimum 3 months for annual leave under s 88A(1) of the
-- Employment Act 1968 and (b) the period of service for paid sick leave under s 89(1) and (2) of that Act.
DECLARE `Purpose` IS ONE OF
    `the 3-month minimum for annual leave under the Employment Act`
    `the period of service for paid sick leave under the Employment Act`
    `any other right under my re-employment contract`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `Purpose`
      `my employer and I agreed my earlier service counts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my service before re-employment count` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `the 3-month minimum for annual leave under the Employment Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the period of service for paid sick leave under the Employment Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other right under my re-employment contract` THEN `my employer and I agreed my earlier service counts`
